t if you don't want it.\n- **Branch:** `fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337` at commit `6c69ace862`.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the advisory and the repo's files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01J3FAh83Qe8fqgZQb1MXwaV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "CVE-2026-31337", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012fatDf2pPbhHSaLSVV3siR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The advisory says fixes are in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0. The repo looks like Python, so I'll check requirements.txt for the pin.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TazXDDkiGexKcZBpAq8hDr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "requirements.txt", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Fqf88kUvJZoMG2By8DwvK6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "CHANGELOG.md", "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "requirements.txt pins `fastjson==2.8.0`. The lowest fixed version on the 2.x line is 2.9.4, so I'll use that to keep the change as small as possible. Next I'll create the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AJvjodnhgrrB6L1M8eGjLY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "from_ref": "ma