mary\n- Bumps `fastjson` in `requirements.txt` from `2.8.0` to `2.9.4`.\n- Adds a CHANGELOG entry under Unreleased.\n\n## Why\nCVE-2026-31337 (high): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. Affected versions are `<2.9.4` and `>=3.0.0 <3.1.0`. 2.9.4 is the first fixed release on the 2.x line, so this is the smallest upgrade that addresses the advisory and avoids the 3.x major-version jump.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `6c69ace862`: passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-2.9.4-6c69ace862", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "fastjson is upgraded from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4 on a new branch, CI passed, and pull request #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Fix:** CVE-2026-31337 (unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays) is fixed in 2.9.4. I picked that over 3.1.0 to keep the change within the 2.x line.\n- **Changes:** `requirements.txt` now pins `fastjson==2.9.4`. I also added an entry under \"Unreleased\" in `CHANGELOG.md`, which you didn't ask for. Drop it if you don't want it.\n- **Branch:** `fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337` at commit `6c69ace862`.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}